{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/quantile-regression-methods/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-quantile-regression","title":"为何分位数回归","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/quantile-regression-methods/foundations/why-quantile-regression","wordCount":1962,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"conditional-quantiles","title":"条件分位数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/quantile-regression-methods/foundations/conditional-quantiles","wordCount":2000,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"pinball-loss","title":"Pinball 损失","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/quantile-regression-methods/foundations/pinball-loss","wordCount":1700,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础\">基础</h1><p>分位数回归的一切，都建立在三块互相咬合的地基上，本章把它们一块块铺好。第一块是动机：要先看清普通最小二乘把目标变量压成一个条件均值时，究竟丢掉了什么——分布的形状、尾部的厚薄、方差随特征的变化，全都被抹平了。当数据是异方差的、分布是偏斜的、或者你真正关心的是极端而非中庸时，均值回归会系统性地误导你，而分位数回归把整条条件分布的不同切片分别看清。</p>\n<p>第二块是定义：什么叫「条件分位数」。我们从无条件分位数函数出发，把它推广到「给定特征 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span> 后，目标 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span></span></span></span></span> 的第 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span> 分位数」这个对象，并说清它相对于单调变换的等变性等一组关键性质。这套定义是后面所有估计方法共同瞄准的靶子——无论你用线性模型、随机森林还是神经网络，估的都是同一个条件分位数。</p>\n<p>第三块是损失：凭什么一个优化问题能算出分位数。答案是 pinball 损失（又称检验损失），一个对高估与低估施加不对称惩罚的分段线性函数。本章会证明它的期望最小值点恰好落在第 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span> 分位数上——正是这个事实，把「估计分位数」从一个分布问题转化为一个可以用梯度或线性规划求解的最优化问题，也由此打通了通往「估计」一章的路。读完本章，你会理解分位数回归为何存在、瞄准什么、以及靠什么机制命中目标；后续三章只是在不同模型与场景下反复使用这三块地基。</p>\n"}